# Local dev config
.claude/

# Real secrets. The service_role key must never reach the browser or
# the repo — it bypasses every row level security policy.
.env

# config.js is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It holds the Supabase URL and the *anon* key. The anon key is
# published to every visitor's browser by design; it is what the site
# uses to read content. Security comes from the row level security
# policies in supabase.sql and admin-schema.sql, not from hiding it.
#
# Keeping it out of the repo meant a fresh clone or an automated deploy
# produced a site that silently fell back to placeholder content.
